    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "Both functions are implemented in `app/network.py`. The 3 existing tests pass (none of them covers the two new functions), and I checked the new code with a stub transport.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`** installs a client factory with huggingface_hub's `set_client_factory`. Every `HfApi` instance then shares one client with:\n- the timeouts you asked for (connect 5s; read, write and pool 60s);\n- the `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` header, added to the headers huggingface_hub sets on each request (user agent, auth and so on);\n- your `transport`, when one is given;\n- huggingface_hub's own settings: its request hook (offline mode, request IDs) and following redirects.\n\n**One thing to know:** huggingface_hub 2.0.0 uses `httpx2`, and `HfApi.model_info` always passes `timeout=None`. `httpx2` reads that as \"no timeout at all\", so a timeout set only on the client would have been switched off for those calls. To prevent that, the client uses a small subclass, `_HubClient`, that treats `timeout=None` as \"use the client's timeouts\". If a call passes an actual number as its timeout, that number is still used.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** asks for the model info at revision `main` and returns its `sha`. If the Hub can't be reached (a connection failure or timeout, including a dropped connection mid-response), it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`. Every other error still raises, including `RepositoryNotFoundError` and offline mode being enabled.\n\n**Stub-transport check:**\n- The request went to `/api/models/a/b/revision/main`.\n- It had both the `X-Acme-Job` header and huggingface_hub's user agent.\n- Its timeouts were `{'connect': 5.0, 'read': 60.0, 'write': 60.0, 'pool': 60.0}`.\n- A `ConnectError` and a `ReadTimeout` each returned `None` and logged a warning.\n- A 404 raised `RepositoryNotFoundError`.\n\n**Also worth knowing:**\n- The async client (used by `AsyncInferenceClient`, not `HfApi`) isn't configured.\n- I didn't add tests to the suite for the new fun"
  },
